    "result_text": "There's a single test class with one test, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164. Three coordinated changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, so this produces `getTelephoneDisplay`/`setTelephoneDisplay` on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Added a static `formatForDisplay(String e164)` helper that emits `+<countryCode> <national digits grouped in threes>` (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It reuses the existing prefix-free `NATIONAL_DIGITS_BY_COUNTRY_CODE` map (`+61`, `+1`) to recognise the country code, falling back to plain three-digit grouping for unknown codes, and returns `null` for `null` input.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` that derives it on read from the stored raw `telephone` via `TelephoneNormalizer.formatForDisplay(...)`, following the same static-utility expression style used by the mapper's other derived fields (`locality`, `checkDigit`).\n\nThe build regenerates the DTOs and the test suite is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` confirms `$.telephone` = `+61412345678` and `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`.",
